atelier atelier/t261 "A plan in a protected project can never be accepted: planGate runs the ordinary gate on the plan item, whose contributors include atelier/integrator (the integrator's pushes), a reserved actor of no recognised family, and familyRefusal fails every reviewer when any contributor's family is unrecognised; so plan t197, with every part reviewed by another family and integrated, was refused 'needs approval from a model of another family than every contributor' even after gpt-oss-120b approved it (2026-10-07). Also, atelier land on a plan item merges main into the plan's branch, which planGate then refuses (head is not the integration head). Fix: when the plan's head is its integration head, every commit on the branch is a recorded integration of a reviewed part (or a recorded refresh), so the plan item needs no review of its own beyond its parts' (atelier/integrator's merge commits are not contributions); an owner-resolved or unrecorded commit on the branch still needs one. atelier land on a plan item refuses and points at atelier merge PLAN --head INTEGRATION_HEAD (a stale branch takes main by plan refresh)"
